    q: 'What is a melanocortin antagonist?',
    a: 'A melanocortin antagonist binds one or more of the five melanocortin receptors and blocks them so the natural activator (α-MSH or ACTH) cannot switch the receptor on. Some go further: AgRP is also an inverse agonist at MC4R, pushing the receptor below its resting activity. Antagonists are the mirror image of agonists such as setmelanotide or afamelanotide.',
