    q: 'Are any melanocortin antagonists FDA-approved?',
    a: 'Not yet as purpose-built melanocortin antagonists. The clinical antagonists — TCMCB07 for cachexia, atumelnant for CAH/Cushing’s, and the discontinued PF-07258669 — remain investigational. SHU9119 is a research tool, not a medicine.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is an antagonist different from an inverse agonist?',
    a: 'A neutral antagonist occupies the receptor and blocks the agonist without changing the receptor’s baseline activity. An inverse agonist actively suppresses constitutive (agonist-independent) signalling. AgRP behaves as an inverse agonist at MC4R; PF-07258669 was designed as a neutral antagonist.',
