  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'A melanocortin antagonist blocks one or more of MC1R–MC5R so the natural agonist cannot activate it — the opposite of setmelanotide, afamelanotide and the rest of the agonist field.',
      'The body already makes two: AgRP (hunger — blocks MC3R/MC4R, and is an inverse agonist at MC4R) and ASIP/agouti (pigment — blocks MC1R).',
      'SHU9119 is the classic research antagonist that proved blocking central MC4R drives eating; it is a lab tool, not a medicine.',
      'Clinical antagonists aim at two problems of excess tone: MC4R blockers for cachexia (TCMCB07; the discontinued PF-07258669) and the MC2R blocker atumelnant for CAH and ACTH-dependent Cushing’s.',
